1
00:00:00,480 --> 00:00:02,340
A curve is one of the first ideas in

2
00:00:02,340 --> 00:00:05,144
geometry. It is a drawing made without lifting the

3
00:00:05,144 --> 00:00:08,000
pencil from the paper. Some curves close up, and

4
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:10,972
some stay open; and a closed curve separates the

5
00:00:10,972 --> 00:00:13,330
plane into an inside and an outside. Let us

6
00:00:13,330 --> 00:00:16,571
learn how to tell them apart.

7
00:00:17,227 --> 00:00:19,969
Imagine drawing with a pencil, and never lifting it

8
00:00:19,969 --> 00:00:22,559
from the paper. You might draw a wavy path,

9
00:00:22,559 --> 00:00:26,327
or a loop, or a path that crosses itself.

10
00:00:26,327 --> 00:00:29,611
And here is a surprise: in geometry, even a

11
00:00:29,611 --> 00:00:31,872
straight line is a curve. So a curve is

12
00:00:31,872 --> 00:00:37,058
any figure drawn in one continuous stroke, without lifting the pencil.

13
00:00:37,680 --> 00:00:40,230
Now ask the first question: does the path close?

14
00:00:40,230 --> 00:00:43,040
Look at this wavy path. Its two ends stay

15
00:00:43,040 --> 00:00:46,440
apart, so it is an open curve. Now look

16
00:00:46,440 --> 00:00:48,337
at this loop. The pencil comes all the way

17
00:00:48,337 --> 00:00:51,060
back to its starting point, so the path closes.

18
00:00:51,060 --> 00:00:52,611
That is a closed curve.

19
00:00:53,147 --> 00:00:57,147
The second question is: does the path cross itself?

20
00:00:57,147 --> 00:01:00,275
This loop never crosses itself, so it is a

21
00:01:00,275 --> 00:01:05,207
simple curve. But this figure crosses itself, right here,

22
00:01:05,207 --> 00:01:08,087
where the two parts meet. So it is not

23
00:01:08,087 --> 00:01:10,040
simple. A simple curve is simply one that does

24
00:01:10,040 --> 00:01:11,538
not cross itself.

25
00:01:12,240 --> 00:01:15,453
These are two different questions. This wavy path is

26
00:01:15,453 --> 00:01:19,407
open, because its ends stay apart, and simple, because

27
00:01:19,407 --> 00:01:24,940
it never crosses itself. This oval is closed, and

28
00:01:24,940 --> 00:01:26,863
it is simple too. But this figure is closed

29
00:01:26,863 --> 00:01:30,100
and it crosses itself, so it is not simple.

30
00:01:30,100 --> 00:01:32,032
Open or closed, and simple or not simple, are

31
00:01:32,032 --> 00:01:34,271
two separate questions.

32
00:01:34,910 --> 00:01:37,550
Now watch what a closed curve does. It is

33
00:01:37,550 --> 00:01:40,570
like the boundary wall of a park. The wall

34
00:01:40,570 --> 00:01:44,330
splits the plane into three parts: the inside, which

35
00:01:44,330 --> 00:01:47,135
we call the interior; the wall itself, the boundary;

36
00:01:47,135 --> 00:01:50,723
and the outside, the exterior. To get from outside

37
00:01:50,723 --> 00:01:54,141
the park to inside, you must cross the boundary.

38
00:01:54,752 --> 00:01:57,232
So when you see a closed figure, ask: where

39
00:01:57,232 --> 00:02:00,852
is each point? A point inside is in the

40
00:02:00,852 --> 00:02:04,166
interior. A point exactly on the edge is on

41
00:02:04,166 --> 00:02:07,983
the boundary. And a point outside is in the exterior.

42
00:02:08,619 --> 00:02:10,086
Now we can say what a region is. The

43
00:02:10,086 --> 00:02:14,019
region is the interior and the boundary taken together.

44
00:02:14,019 --> 00:02:17,859
The interior alone is not the whole region; the

45
00:02:17,859 --> 00:02:21,139
edge is part of the region too. Region equals

46
00:02:21,139 --> 00:02:22,770
interior plus boundary.

47
00:02:23,426 --> 00:02:25,504
One more step connects curves to the shapes we

48
00:02:25,504 --> 00:02:28,416
study next. If a simple closed curve is made

49
00:02:28,416 --> 00:02:31,246
of straight line segments, it is called a polygon.

50
00:02:31,246 --> 00:02:34,026
So a polygon is a special kind of simple

51
00:02:34,026 --> 00:02:37,757
closed figure, and we will meet it very soon.

52
00:02:38,378 --> 00:02:42,112
Your turn. Four quick checks. For each diagram, say

53
00:02:42,112 --> 00:02:44,991
whether the curve is open or closed, and simple

54
00:02:44,991 --> 00:02:48,194
or not simple. A wavy path with two free

55
00:02:48,194 --> 00:02:54,898
ends. A closed oval. A path that crosses itself.

56
00:02:54,898 --> 00:02:57,268
And last of all: in this closed figure, point

57
00:02:57,268 --> 00:03:00,095
P is inside, point Q is on the edge,

58
00:03:00,095 --> 00:03:03,769
and point R is outside. Classify P, Q and R.

59
00:03:14,771 --> 00:03:17,180
The first is open, because its ends do not

60
00:03:17,180 --> 00:03:21,831
meet, and simple, because it never crosses itself. The

61
00:03:21,831 --> 00:03:25,351
second is closed and simple: a smooth oval. The

62
00:03:25,351 --> 00:03:28,591
third crosses itself, so it is not simple. And

63
00:03:28,591 --> 00:03:31,851
in the last figure, P is in the interior,

64
00:03:31,851 --> 00:03:35,282
Q is on the boundary, and R is in the exterior.

65
00:03:35,898 --> 00:03:38,309
One last look. A curve is drawn without lifting

66
00:03:38,309 --> 00:03:41,193
the pencil. If the ends stay apart, it is

67
00:03:41,193 --> 00:03:44,818
open; if they join, it is closed. And if

68
00:03:44,818 --> 00:03:48,515
it never crosses itself, it is simple. A closed

69
00:03:48,515 --> 00:03:51,804
curve gives us interior, boundary and exterior, and the

70
00:03:51,804 --> 00:03:55,278
region is the interior plus the boundary. Draw, classify,

71
00:03:55,278 --> 00:03:58,610
locate. Thank you for watching, and see you in

72
00:03:58,610 --> 00:03:59,569
the next lesson.
